WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.073
The man sitting in front of the fire was once more a younger version of Scrooge.

2
00:00:06.074 --> 00:00:10.737
However, the man had aged since the party at Fezziwig's.

3
00:00:10.738 --> 00:00:14.954
His face no longer looked shy and eager.

4
00:00:14.955 --> 00:00:21.077
Now there was a hardness in his eyes and around his mouth.

5
00:00:21.078 --> 00:00:25.164
The young woman beside him had tears in her eyes.

6
00:00:25.165 --> 00:00:30.341
Scrooge felt his heart twist with pain as he looked at lovely Belle.

7
00:00:30.342 --> 00:00:35.074
He had been in love with her long ago.

8
00:00:35.075 --> 00:00:39.683
"A new idol has displaced me in your heart," Belle said.

9
00:00:39.684 --> 00:00:46.683
"I hope it can cheer and comfort you in the future, as I would have tried to do."

10
00:00:46.684 --> 00:00:56.392
Ebenezer looked confused. "I don't understand. What idol has displaced you?"

11
00:00:56.393 --> 00:00:59.951
"Money," Belle said sadly.

12
00:00:59.952 --> 00:01:06.684
Ebenezer scoffed. "That's the way of the world, Belle.

13
00:01:06.685 --> 00:01:14.882
Soft-hearted people might say it's wrong to think about money, but nobody wants to be poor, do they?"

14
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:21.869
"No, but it's possible to fear poverty too much," she said.

15
00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:25.946
"You've set aside all your other hopes and dreams.

16
00:01:25.947 --> 00:01:32.226
Now your only passion is making money, more and more money."

17
00:01:32.227 --> 00:01:38.468
Ebenezer shrugged. "That's because I'm wiser than most people in this world.

18
00:01:38.469 --> 00:01:43.923
And you're wrong to say that money is my only passion.

19
00:01:43.924 --> 00:01:48.519
My love for you hasn't changed at all."

20
00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:54.775
She shook her head. "When we first met, we were both poor but content.

21
00:01:54.776 --> 00:02:02.366
But you have changed, Ebenezer, which means your feelings toward me have changed too.

22
00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:08.179
Back when we met, you were a completely different man."

23
00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:11.751
"I was a boy," he said impatiently.

24
00:02:11.752 --> 00:02:15.656
"I didn't understand wealth back then."

25
00:02:15.657 --> 00:02:19.682
"It's something much more than that," Belle said.

26
00:02:19.683 --> 00:02:23.659
"That's why I've reached another sad conclusion."

27
00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:27.179
"What is it?" Ebenezer said.

28
00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.272
A tear slipped down Belle's cheek.

29
00:02:30.273 --> 00:02:35.431
"You once promised to marry me and take care of me.

30
00:02:35.432 --> 00:02:39.740
But I must release you from your promise."

31
00:02:39.741 --> 00:02:44.298
"What?" Ebenezer looked startled.

32
00:02:44.299 --> 00:02:50.978
"I don't want you to release me from my promise. So why are you doing this?"

33
00:02:50.979 --> 00:02:57.613
Belle sighed. "Because you aren't the same man who made that promise.

34
00:02:57.614 --> 00:03:01.131
Imagine if we were to meet for the first time today.

35
00:03:01.132 --> 00:03:05.451
Would you bother trying to win my heart?"

36
00:03:05.452 --> 00:03:13.378
Ebenezer hesitated. "Of course I would! You think I wouldn't?"

37
00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:17.077
"I wish I believed you would still try to win my heart.

38
00:03:17.078 --> 00:03:20.823
But I believe you would never choose a poor girl today.

39
00:03:20.824 --> 00:03:25.939
You'd never choose a girl with no family money to bring to a marriage.

40
00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:30.901
Not when you value everything in the world by how much it costs."

41
00:03:30.902 --> 00:03:32.890
"Belle, I . . ."

42
00:03:32.891 --> 00:03:38.660
Belle took a deep breath.

43
00:03:38.661 --> 00:03:44.396
"Therefore, with a full heart, I release you.

44
00:03:44.397 --> 00:03:48.396
May you be happy in the life you have chosen."

45
00:03:48.397 --> 00:03:53.076
Ebenezer opened his mouth again and looked ready to protest.

46
00:03:53.077 --> 00:04:01.647
But at the sight of Belle's determined face, he merely nodded and left.

47
00:04:01.648 --> 00:04:05.879
Scrooge watched Belle collapse in tears.

48
00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:09.525
"Spirit, show me no more!" he cried.

49
00:04:09.526 --> 00:04:15.257
"Why do you delight in torturing me? Please take me home!"

50
00:04:15.258 --> 00:04:25.130
The ghost stretched out its finger. "We must see one more shadow."

51
00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:28.219
Scrooge found himself in a different room.

52
00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:34.288
A beautiful young woman sat near the fire, and for a moment, he thought she was Belle.

53
00:04:34.289 --> 00:04:37.993
Then he spied a middle-aged woman nearby.

54
00:04:37.994 --> 00:04:43.274
That was Belle, and he guessed that the younger woman was her daughter.

55
00:04:43.275 --> 00:04:49.155
The room was in an uproar, with several children racing around shouting and laughing.

56
00:04:49.156 --> 00:04:55.552
Scrooge was so agitated by seeing Belle again that he didn't bother trying to count her children.

57
00:04:55.553 --> 00:05:03.291
Instead he watched as Belle and her oldest daughter laughed at the younger ones' noisy antics.

58
00:05:03.292 --> 00:05:10.955
Suddenly the door flew open, and a smiling man entered, his arms loaded with holiday gifts.

59
00:05:10.956 --> 00:05:18.131
The children raced over, nearly smothering him with hugs while shouting joyful greetings.

60
00:05:18.132 --> 00:05:23.493
The man finally managed to make his way past them to Belle.

61
00:05:23.494 --> 00:05:27.799
Leaning down, he gave her a fond kiss.

62
00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:33.785
Scrooge couldn't help imagining himself in the other man's place.

63
00:05:33.786 --> 00:05:39.879
"What if I had married Belle, as we'd planned long ago?" he thought.

64
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:46.350
"What if I were the one coming home to a house full of children who were happy to see me?"

65
00:05:46.351 --> 00:05:49.360
Scrooge closed his eyes.

66
00:05:49.361 --> 00:05:55.040
"Stop!" he cried, trying to banish such thoughts from his mind.

67
00:05:55.041 --> 00:06:00.749
"Spirit, I don't want to see any more of this scene!"

68
00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:05.088
But the ghost sounded unmoved by Scrooge's pain.

69
00:06:05.089 --> 00:06:16.722
"You must see more. And you will see it."

